WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.090
c. AD 1 · Llandough hill, above the River
Ely

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:09.560
Spoken in Welsh, the living descendant of
the Brittonic they spoke

3
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.338
[in Welsh] The pit is already dug. We lay
them here.

4
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.171
[in Welsh] Gently, now. Cross the arms.
Let them look up the slope.

5
00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.486
[in Welsh] So young. The wind is cold up
here.

6
00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:49.636
[in Welsh] Stay with me a while. Then we
fill it in, together.

